    "result_text": "There is only one test class, and the full suite is green.\n\nDone. The change is implemented:\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n- **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct expression mapping that derives the tier: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE` (with null-safe guards on both fields).\n\nThe tier is computed at serialization time in the mapper (like the existing `membershipNumber`/`displayName`/`initials` derived fields), so it surfaces consistently on both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}`. Both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
